== Strategy ==
* As Tainted ??? begins with a low tears stat, it is almost required to rely on poops in the early game. The player should not be scared to use poops, as Tainted ??? will naturally create many poops as he deals damage, especially in boss battles. However, it may be best to save more powerful poops or poop synergies, such as White Poops and brown creep, for more difficult situations such as boss battles.
** Tainted ???'s low tears also makes tears up items like {{I|Torn Photo}} very beneficial.
* More than any other type of poop, it can be beneficial to use Hold on bomb poops for utility purposes, such as finding {{r|Secret Room}}s or reaching pickups behind rocks.
** Alternatively, flaming poops can be used in conjunction with stinky poops/farts to blow things up without using bombs. The stinky poop/fart can be used next to what the player wants to blow up, then the flaming poop can be thrown at it to create an explosion. This can also be done by throwing stinky poops at a fire or flaming poop, though care must be taken as it is easy to get caught in the ensuing explosion if the player does not move out of the way quickly enough.
* If playing in [[Greed Mode]], it's best to try to complete all waves in one sitting as exiting the main room will cause all poops and creep to disappear.
* '''Almost anything''' that resembles a fire can cause toxic clouds created by farts and Stinky Poop to explode. This includes {{e|Fire Place}}s, fires shot by enemies (such as {{E|Candler}}s, {{E|Fire Worm}}s, and {{E|Revenant}}s), and fires created by Tainted ??? (such as with {{i|The Candle}}, {{I|Ghost Pepper}}, and {{I|Bird's Eye}}). Extra caution must be taken to stay away from gas clouds if playing with or around fires.
** {{I|Urn of Souls}} is a notable exception to this.
** Stinky Poops can intentionally be thrown at blue/purple fireplaces to blow them up for the chance to gain {{e|Soul Heart}}s. Be careful not to destroy [[Angel|Angel statues]] next to them if they’re in an {{R|Angel Room}} if you do not wish to fight the angel.

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}} allows Tainted ??? to hold up to 29 poops in the poop counter.
* {{I|Ankh}} Causes Tainted ??? to respawn as himself instead of ???.

=== Good Items ===
* Items that break obstacles such as{{I|Bob's Rotten Head}}, {{I|Mr. Boom}}, or {{I|Notched Axe}} lets Tainted ??? break open tinted rocks, secret rooms, and other obstacles without needing to save a bomb poop.
* {{t|Apple of Sodom}} turns useless red hearts into friendly spiders.
* {{t|Blessed Penny}} can sometimes spawn half soul hearts on the collection of coins, which can occasionally be dropped by thrown poops.
* {{t|Burnt Penny}}: Grants generated pennies a chance to drop large poop pickups.
* {{t|Butt Penny}}: Grants generated poops a chance to drop a penny.
* {{I|The Candle}}/{{I|Red Candle}} allows Tainted ??? to ignite gas at will and from a safe distance, making him less reliant on poop bombs and explosive diarrhea.
* {{I|D20}} become more effective since Tainted ??? could spawn more pickups naturally.
* With {{I|Gnawed Leaf}}, poops held above Tainted ???'s head can still damage enemies while invulnerable.
* {{I|Dirty Mind}} benefits Tainted ??? immensely, allowing him to amass an army of [[Familiar#Dips|Dip Familiars]] for free simply by breaking his poops.
* {{I|Mom's Bracelet}} allows Tainted ??? to pick up an already-placed poop and put it in a different spot (e.g. putting white poop in favorable spot to fight a boss).
* {{t|Petrified Poop}} is naturally a good trinket for Tainted ???, as his heavy reliance on poop makes it easy to obtain pickups. Note that pickups will only drop from normal and corny poops, and not from other poop varieties.
* {{I|Remote Detonator}} allows for more controlled usage of the Explosive Diarrhea poop, and allows for the player to potentially save themselves from a fart chain explosion.
* {{I|Rock Bottom}} is extremely strong with Tainted ???, allowing him to permanently gain the stat increases gained from standing in his Brown Creep and White Poop auras.
* {{I|Tech.5}} patches up Tainted ???'s low fire rate, as the technology laser fires around 2.5 times a second.
* {{t|Lost Cork}} makes the Brown Creep bigger, allowing to maintain it's bonuses with slightly more maneuverability.
* {{t|Gigante Bean}} increases the size of gas clouds and farts.
* {{t|Lil Larva}} spawns a blue fly when a poop is destroyed.
* [[Tear_Effects#Homing|Homing Tears]] allow you to reliably benefit from brown creep's damage and fire rate bonus as White Poop is quite rare.

=== Bad Items ===
* With {{I|Bird's Eye}} or {{I|Ghost Pepper}}, the explosion might be very hard to avoid if your current poop is farting, since farting guarantees to spawn fire. The only surefire way to not harm yourself using a fart is to move in one direction constantly while farting.
* {{I|Finger!}} will harm special poops whenever it's pointed at them, forcing the player to take special care to not look or turn to the poop to avoid weakening them accidentally.
* Items that directly add Red Hearts to the health bar, such as {{i|Yum Heart}}, {{i|Yuck Heart}}, or full health [[pill]]s, are useless. However, eternal hearts still act as an extra half a heart and become a full soul heart at the end of the floor, making {{I|Prayer Card}} viable.
* Items that cause Isaac to shoot tears in different directions, such as {{i|Mom's Eye}}, makes it much harder to capitalize on corny or holy poops, as there is a high chance of them breaking if Isaac is firing near them.
* {{M|Blood Donation Machine}}s and {{M|Devil Beggar}}s are riskier, as they deplete health that is harder to replenish.
* {{I|Book of Virtues}} wisps may break special poops if not careful.
* {{i|Guppy's Paw}}, since it requires Red Hearts to convert, would be a useless item to hold (but should still be picked up and swapped back to get credit towards the [[Guppy]] transformation).
* {{i|Holy Water}} tends to destroy poops as soon as they are thrown unless the player has careful timing and aim.
* {{t|Judas' Tongue}} doesn't lower the price of Soul Heart Devil deals.
* {{i|Little C.H.A.D.}} is useless unless paired with {{i|Dark Bum}}, where it becomes very useful.
* {{i|Marked}}, while allowing the player to have slightly more control over the directions that the poops are thrown, also often makes it difficult to avoid immediately breaking them. This can be especially harsh when trying to use holy poops, as the firing rate increase will almost guarantee the poop being immediately destroyed.
* {{I|Tiny Planet}} can cause the player to accidentally break special poops while trying to fire. This becomes less impactful with items which replace tears, like {{I|Technology}}.

